{
  "id": 8,
  "title": "Describing things",
  "goal": "Describe people and things by colour, size and quality, and compare them.",
  "intro": "Malayalam adjectives are easy in one way — they **never agree** with the noun in gender or number — and slightly tricky in another: many have two forms, one used *before* a noun (വലിയ വീട് 'a big house') and one used as a predicate (വീട് വലുതാണ് 'the house is big').\n\nMany 'adjectives' are really nouns: ഭംഗി 'beauty', ഭാരം 'weight', ചുവപ്പ് 'redness'. You describe with them by adding **-ഉള്ള** 'having' (ഭംഗിയുള്ള 'beautiful') or using them with ആണ് / ഉണ്ട്.",
